actual_result: "Merged in #218 as 094b998; checks successful at head 9984f62: CodeQL, audit-windows, codeql, release-gate (bun), release-gate (npm), semgrep-cloud-platform/scan, test (22), test (26)."
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T10:37:34.625Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Failure -> cause -> fix: action native/harness test expects numeric tokenBudget 4000 to refuse -> GH-1665 string coercion -> prove numeric 4000 succeeds and replace the refusal with Infinity, retaining invalid JSON/schema/size and budget-boundary cases. Follow-through numeric tokenBudget 1 now reaches follow_through_budget -> assert that exact category and replace raw-type refusal with malformed integer spelling. Removed CLI-unreachable raw string-type guards in both adapters; strict public data parsers remain. Ordinary document files instead fail extension_read_output_invalid before the owned renderer: undocumented upstream candidate, reproduced with a minimal synthetic extension; harness succeeds but native CLI exits 2 for missing rows. Compatibility fix retains real structured rows internally and emits only the separate bounded file receipt. The new migration document records exact version, harness call, native command, observations and expected behavior; no upstream issue filed."
  "2026-11-14T10:43:17.780Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Final focused evidence: native action and follow-through cases pass 2/2 after adapter/type-test migration. The corrected file-summary case passes through pm test --run --only-last with real native JSON/TOON output, nonempty files and no leaked row collections or internal markers. The disposable behavioral revert restored only the original index adapters while retaining current tests/dependencies: ordinary file output fails extension_read_output_invalid; the fixed worktree passes. npm/Bun typecheck, build:test and docstrings (200 declarations) pass. No standalone lint script is declared. Full npm/Bun release checks are queued serially at unchanged thresholds; prior native action scenario took 232 seconds under shared load. Original current-pin baseline failed all 3 reported cases. Minimal synthetic harness/native reproduction confirms the undocumented host file-receipt mismatch."
  "2026-11-14T11:07:26.201Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Broader release matrix caught a receipt-compatibility regression in the first adapter change: direct SDK consumers require ok, format and output alongside the host validation rows. Preserve rendered receipt metadata first, overlay structured rows so count fields cannot replace declared row arrays, and keep the separately rendered compact file receipt. Existing divergence, since and all-command-family acceptance tests fail with the previous helper and cover this correction without lowering any assertion or threshold. Stopped the failed broad run and am verifying those SDK cases plus the native compact receipt before restarting exact-head release gates."
  "2026-11-14T11:10:32.786Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Receipt compatibility correction verified: the SDK all-command-family output matrix, direct divergence text/slack receipt case, and native compact file-output case pass 3/3, zero failures/cancellations/skips (138 seconds). The prior helper fails existing ok/format/output assertions in the release matrix; the corrected merge preserves that metadata while structured row arrays take precedence over count fields. Native emitted file receipts remain bounded and contain no internal markers or row arrays. This is the behavioral revert proof for the correction. Full exact-head gates will restart after this commit; no assertions or thresholds were weakened."
  "2026-11-14T11:27:47.361Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Additional compatibility evidence for the undocumented host receipt change: installed the published CLI 2026.11.7 in a separate synthetic consumer and ran the fixed built extension through native JSON and TOON file-output commands. Both exit 0, write nonempty documents, retain ok/format/output, and expose no internal markers or row collections; the TOON receipt is 106 bytes. Together with current CLI 2026.11.14 native acceptance this verifies the compatibility adapter under both host behaviors. The migration document now retains this result. CI for the source head is queued; its exact run is https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/43588852975. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-11-14T13:02:55.010Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"The full gate exposed one additional receipt-metadata regression in the compatibility merge: brief since empty-window SDK receipts lost explicit truncated:false because the structured summary owns truncated:undefined. Focused unchanged test reproduces 0/1 with an exact undefined-versus-false assertion. The failed full run was stopped before changing source. The fix gives receipt scalars precedence while restoring structured row arrays over compact counts for host validation; no assertion or threshold changes. This existing failing case is the behavioral revert proof."
  "2026-11-14T13:05:33.037Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Final scalar-precedence correction passes the existing SDK all-family matrix, divergence receipt, empty-window delta receipt and native document-file case: 4/4 tests with zero failures/cancellations/skips (72 seconds). The new linked empty-window check passes 1/1 through pm test --run --only-last --progress. npm/Bun typecheck, build:test and 200-declaration docstring gate pass. The pre-fix function fails the unchanged empty-window assertion (undefined versus false), while the corrected function retains rows for native validation and explicit receipt scalars. Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates will run serially after Context; no in-flight suite observed a source edit."
  "2026-11-14T13:51:57.888Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"The final npm release gate reached a separate timing blocker: the existing handoff-repair 500-sequence model hit its explicit 900000ms timeout after the sibling 500-sequence coverage model passed. No assertion failure was reported before that timeout. The known-red npm process subtree was stopped (exit 143); sources were not edited during the run. All four focused receipt regressions and the linked empty-window case remain passing. A separate unchanged Bun release gate is now attempted; the model corpus, timeout and coverage thresholds are retained. Full npm certification remains outstanding in CI."
  "2026-11-14T14:07:14.049Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Final source commit 4a19f2c7e871e12d72db7d40e32b447a0ba81d10 retains passing focused receipt regressions 4/4 plus the linked empty-window check 1/1, typed action/follow-through cases 2/2, and native JSON/TOON file acceptance under published CLI 2026.11.7 and current CLI 2026.11.14. npm/Bun typecheck, build:test and 200-declaration docstring checks pass. Full release attempts are incomplete: npm handoff-repair 500-sequence model hit its existing 900-second test limit; Bun action replay 500-sequence corpus hit its existing 300-second limit. Each known-red subtree was stopped with exit 143; no assertion failure was reported before either timeout. Workloads, timeouts and coverage thresholds remain unchanged, and no complete coverage pass is claimed. Source-head CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/43599123171 and CodeQL run 43599122947 were cancelled and are missing evidence. Final-head CI will be inspected after this evidence-only publication. The shared-runner hold was honored; the item stays released and in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-14T14:55:50.906Z",codex-toolchain-1114a,"Failure | Cause (host contract) | Fix\n--- | --- | ---\nnative non-git CLI and injected action command emit bounded JSON/TOON and typed usage errors | GH-1665: numeric tokenBudget is normalized as CLI string input. | Accept numeric 4000; replace its old refusal with Infinity, retaining malformed JSON, request-schema, size and budget refusals and no-write checks.\nreal native non-git follow-through CLI emits JSON/TOON and injected handlers share the schema | GH-1665: numeric 1 now reaches the handler budget boundary. | Assert the budget refusal and retain a separate invalid integer spelling; remove CLI-unreachable raw string-type guards from the adapters.\nordinary document files preserve summary output | Native host validates declared row collections before the owned file formatter; no migration note announces this receipt change. | Retain rows internally and emit only the compact receipt. Preserve receipt scalar defaults, including truncated:false, while row arrays take precedence over compact counts. Native CLI 2026.11.7 and 2026.11.14 acceptance passes.\n\nContract reference: [pm-cli 2026.11.8 migration entries](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#2026118---2026-11-08). Full gate results and timing limits are recorded in the preceding validation receipts. No workload or coverage threshold was lowered. This final comment makes the failure/cause/fix mapping explicit; source files are unchanged."
